    {
      "text": "5.1. Empirical False Positive Rate",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        371.8600769042969,
        277.8656005859375,
        381.54736328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We start by examining the tightness of the reachable set approximation in example 2 through",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        393.5430908203125,
        522.0549926757812,
        403.2303771972656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the empirical measurement of false positives.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        407.09210205078125,
        303.63287353515625,
        416.7793884277344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We compare the empirical Christoffel polynomial with other prevalent nonconformity",
      "bbox": [
        106.93600463867188,
        421.86309814453125,
        522.049072265625,
        431.5503845214844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "functions: one-class SVM, Isolation Forest (Liu et al., 2008), and Local Outlier Factor",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        435.412109375,
        522.0439453125,
        445.0993957519531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(LOF), as shown in Figure 6. Only the approximation using LOF seems comparable to",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        448.96112060546875,
        522.0548095703125,
        458.6484069824219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that of the Christoffel polynomial, while Isolation Forest exhibits significant variability",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        462.5111083984375,
        522.07666015625,
        472.1983947753906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "depending on the random seed.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        476.06011962890625,
        239.5092315673828,
        485.7474060058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To gauge the number of false positives and assess the accuracy of the reachable set ap-",
      "bbox": [
        106.93600463867188,
        490.83111572265625,
        521.994384765625,
        500.5184020996094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "proximation, we generated 10,000 uniformly distributed samples within the domain [−4, 4]2.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        502.4607849121094,
        522.002685546875,
        514.0674438476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The false-positive rate was empirically determined for various degrees d, as shown in Ta-",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        517.9291381835938,
        521.9954833984375,
        527.616455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ble 2. As observed in earlier plots, a higher degree results in a more accurate fit of the",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        531.4781494140625,
        522.0221557617188,
        541.1654663085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reachable set.",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        545.0281372070312,
        155.9345703125,
        554.7154541015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The false-positive rates for the other algorithms can also be observed in",
      "bbox": [
        164.7054901123047,
        545.0281372070312,
        522.0112915039062,
        554.7154541015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Table 2 for varying sizes of the training and calibration sets. Consistent with the findings",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        558.5771484375,
        522.0657348632812,
        568.2644653320312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "from the Figure 6, only the LOF provides results that are comparable in quality to those",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        572.1260986328125,
        522.0657348632812,
        581.8134155273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "obtained using the Christoffel polynomial.",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        585.6751098632812,
        291.0982971191406,
        595.3624267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To further demonstrate the effectiveness of the empirical Christoffel polynomial as a",
      "bbox": [
        106.93597412109375,
        600.4461059570312,
        522.0053100585938,
        610.1334228515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "non-conformity function, we examine its robustness in the presence of outliers within the",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        613.9951171875,
        522.0438842773438,
        623.6824340820312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "training set. Although the theoretical guarantees discussed in this article and in general",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        627.5451049804688,
        522.0547485351562,
        637.232421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conformal prediction hold for any choice of non-conformity function, even with outliers in",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        641.0941162109375,
        522.0874633789062,
        650.7814331054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the training set, the presence of these outliers can impact the accuracy of the model. To",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        654.6431274414062,
        522.0110473632812,
        664.3304443359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "compare the empirical Christoffel polynomial with LOF, we conducted two experiments. In",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        668.192138671875,
        522.0220336914062,
        677.8794555664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the first experiment, we considered the region [−1, 1]2 as the reachable set to approximate.",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        677.7830810546875,
        522.0089721679688,
        691.4284057617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We focused on comparing the performance of the algorithms under the presence of outliers",
      "bbox": [
        89.99996948242188,
        695.2911376953125,
        522.0330200195312,
        704.9784545898438
      ],
      "direction": [
